WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.588
The change advisory board
authorizes production changes.

2
00:00:03.588 --> 00:00:07.102
But two decisions aren't the
board's: letting a class of change

3
00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:10.899
run without a person, and whether
a change needs reauthorization.

4
00:00:10.899 --> 00:00:15.200
Those are risk decisions, and risk
belongs to the authorizing official.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.150
The quietest way separation
is lost is here.

6
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.519
An approval rule is just configuration,

7
00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.750
and the team that runs the
platform can usually edit it.

8
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.488
So the decision for the board:
any change to approval rules,

9
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:31.225
routing or integrations is a
normal change it authorizes.

10
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:33.687
Nobody changes the gate they pass through.

11
00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:36.600
Next, proving it to an
authorizing official.
